1
00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:07,360
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:07,360
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:14,990
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:14,990
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:22,830
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,210
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,210
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:29,920
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:29,920
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:37,390
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:37,390
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:44,890
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:44,890
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:51,820
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:51,820
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,160
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,160
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,740
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,740
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:03,370
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:03,370
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:03,370 --> 00:01:06,710
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:03,370 --> 00:01:06,710
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,090
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,090
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:14,840
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:14,840
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,590
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,590
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:22,310
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:22,310
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:25,940
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:25,940
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:29,690
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:29,690
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:38,740
Good morning, Shinji. How are you?

37
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:40,160
I'm getting used to it.

38
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,740
I think it's not bad.

39
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:43,160
That's good.

40
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:45,580
Have you memorized the positions
of all the Eva emergence points,

41
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:49,880
emergency power junctions, armament
buildings, and recovery zones?

42
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,250
I think so.

43
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:52,550
Then, I'll review it one more time.

44
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:56,260
Normally the Eva runs off electricity
provided by an umbilical cable.

45
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:59,180
In emergencies, it can switch to
an internal battery,

46
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:02,010
with an active life of one minute at full power,

47
00:02:02,010 --> 00:02:05,350
and no more than five minutes in
the minimal activity gain mode.

48
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:08,100
This is the limitations of
our current technology.

49
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,850
Do you understand?

50
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:10,860
Yes.

51
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:14,280
Now let's continue from where we left off
yesterday. We'll initiate Induction Mode.

52
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:20,870
Position the target in the center,

53
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,740
then switch "on".

54
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:28,870
Calm down. Position the target in the center.

55
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:29,500
Switch...

56
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:36,010
Next!

57
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:48,230
But I'm surprised that Shinji
agreed to pilot it.

58
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:50,560
He simply does what he's told to do.

59
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,770
Maybe that's his way of getting through life.

60
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:00,320
Target in the center, pull the switch.

61
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:03,530
Target in the center, pull the switch.

62
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,870
Target in the center, pull the switch.

63
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:10,540
Target in the center, pull the switch.

64
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:13,500
Target in the center...

65
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:17,170
EPISODE THREE
THE SILENT PHONE

66
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:21,840
<i><i>And now, from Tokyo we go to
Miss Natsuko Shinohara in Matsuzaki.</i></i>

67
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:25,640
<i><i>Good morning, this is Shinohara.
Guess what?</i></i>

68
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:29,730
<i><i>Today I'm in Matsuzaki in West lzu
for a little scuba diving!</i></i>

69
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:32,980
<i><i>Today's forecast is sunny, with an
estimated high of 32 degrees C.</i></i>

70
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:33,730
Miss Misato, it's morning already.

71
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:37,070
<i><i>We have hot days all year now,
but we used to have four seasons:</i></i>

72
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:37,730
I just got back from night duty.

73
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,360
<i><i>Spring, Summer, Fall and Winter.</i></i>

74
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:42,660
I don't have to go to work until this
evening, so please, let me sleep.

75
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:45,280
<i><i>We never see snow these days,
instead, due to the recent warmth,</i></i>

76
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:45,120
I see. I'll go.

77
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,780
<i><i>aquatic life has been coming back
little by little.</i></i>

78
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,330
Hey, is today Thursday?

79
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:51,080
<i><i>As you dive into the sea you can
clearly see an abundance of fish.</i></i>

80
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:49,700
Take the burnable trash
to the garbage, please.

81
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:51,620
Yes, Ma'am.

82
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:59,210
<i><i>It makes me think of catching some
for tonight's dinner.</i></i>

83
00:03:52,330 --> 00:03:55,330
So, are you adjusting to school?

84
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,040
Yeah.

85
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,840
Oh, okay. See you later.

86
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:02,050
<i><i>Although the town brings back sad
memories, this is a hot diving spot.</i></i>

87
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,050
I'll see you later.

88
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:18,230
Yes? Hello?

89
00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:20,820
Oh, it's you, Ritsuko.

90
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:23,490
How's it going? Are you getting along
with your boyfriend?

91
00:04:23,490 --> 00:04:25,070
Boyfriend?

92
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:27,120
Oh, you mean Shinji.

93
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,870
Well, he transferred into school two
weeks ago and he hasn't changed.

94
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:32,750
No one ever calls him.

95
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:34,000
Calls him?

96
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,170
Well, since I figured he'd need one,
I gave him a cell phone a while back.

97
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:42,630
I don't think he's ever used it though,
or received any calls.

98
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:47,300
I'm not sure, but I don't think
he has any friends.

99
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:52,100
Well, I would guess that Shinji's not
the sort who makes friends easily.

100
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:55,640
Do you know the fable of the
"Hedgehog's Dilemma"?

101
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,610
Hedgehog? You mean those animals
with the spiny hair?

102
00:04:58,610 --> 00:05:02,530
Even though a hedgehog may wish
to get close to another hedgehog,

103
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:07,030
the closer they get, the more they
injure each other with their spines.

104
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:09,410
It's the same with some humans.

105
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:14,960
Shinji is probably afraid of pain and has
become a coward somewhere in his heart.

106
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:18,380
Well, he'll eventually learn that growing up

107
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:22,000
means getting closer to people
and distancing them,

108
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:26,590
finding a distance where you can avoid
hurting each other too much.

109
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,360
What's up, class rep?

110
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:45,030
Class Daybook

111
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:43,940
Did you give him the printout
I gave you yesterday?

112
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:45,030
What? Well...

113
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:50,370
Well, there wasn't anybody home
at Toji's place.

114
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:53,330
Aida, you're good friends
with Suzuhara, right?

115
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:56,290
He's been absent for two weeks.
Aren't you worried?

116
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:57,960
Do you suppose he's been seriously injured?

117
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:00,500
What? In that robot incident?!

118
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,420
The television report said
that nobody was injured!

119
00:06:02,420 --> 00:06:05,760
No way, you saw the explosion site
on Mount Takanosu, didn't you?

120
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:08,630
Not only were Iruma and
Komatsu dispatched,

121
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:11,510
they brought in troops from
Misawa and Kyushu.

122
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:14,770
There had to have been well over
a couple dozen people injured,

123
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:16,140
and even some killed.

124
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:18,940
Toji!

125
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:20,100
Suzuhara!

126
00:06:21,270 --> 00:06:24,440
Wow, has the class population
dropped or what?

127
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:28,280
They've all evacuated and
transferred to other schools.

128
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:31,370
After all, no one wants to stay after
that fierce battle inside the city.

129
00:06:31,370 --> 00:06:34,080
Yeah, you're probably the only one

130
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:36,120
who's actually enjoyin' the chance
to see a real war.

131
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,290
I suppose so.

132
00:06:37,290 --> 00:06:40,290
So where have you been, Toji?
You were gone for so long.

133
00:06:40,290 --> 00:06:43,630
Did you get caught in the crossfire
or something?

134
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,590
My kid sister did.

135
00:06:47,170 --> 00:06:50,840
She was crushed under a pile of debris.

136
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:54,680
She survived, but she's been
in the hospital ever since.

137
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:58,480
Both my pop and gramps work at the lab,

138
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:01,310
and there's no way they can
leave their posts right now.

139
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:04,770
So, if I ain't with her, she's all alone
at the hospital.

140
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:10,950
Man, that robot's pilot was plain awful!
I'm downright pissed off!

141
00:07:10,950 --> 00:07:13,740
What the hell's the point of
our own guy wreckin' the city?

142
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:17,450
Oh, about the pilot, have you heard the
rumor about the new transfer student?

143
00:07:17,450 --> 00:07:19,250
Transfer student?

144
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:20,210
Him, over there.

145
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:25,540
He transferred here while you were absent.

146
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:28,960
He came right after the incident.
Don't you think that's odd?

147
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:33,590
All rise!

148
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:41,350
And so, humankind was about to face
its greatest trial.

149
00:07:41,350 --> 00:07:43,650
In the last year of the 20th century,

150
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:48,530
the massive meteor from space slammed
into the continent of Antarctica.

151
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:52,530
The continent's ice cap was melted
almost instantaneously.

152
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:55,870
The water level of the oceans rose,
the Earth was thrown off its axis,

153
00:07:55,870 --> 00:08:01,160
and abnormal weather patterns threatened
the lives of all living things.

154
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:08,210
Several thousand species and half of the
world's population were lost for eternity.

155
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:12,340
That was the so-called "Second lmpact".

156
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:15,680
The survivors still had to live through the hell

157
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:19,970
of worldwide economic collapse,
ethnic conflicts, and civil wars.

158
00:08:19,010 --> 00:08:22,810
Is it true that you're the pilot of that robot? Y/N

159
00:08:19,970 --> 00:08:22,640
However, it has been fifteen years since then.

160
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:26,650
In only fifteen years,
we have restored ourselves.

161
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:32,690
This is certainly proof of the human race's
resilience, but even more so,

162
00:08:30,150 --> 00:08:31,740
It's true, isn't it?

163
00:08:32,690 --> 00:08:36,870
it is the fruit of the blood, sweat and tears

164
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:41,660
your fathers and mothers have
dedicated to this cause.

165
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:43,910
What?!

166
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:45,920
Really?! Oh, wow! Cool!

167
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:47,830
I lived in Nebukawa at the time,
which is underwater now...

168
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,630
Really, the new student was?

169
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:49,840
Hey, you guys!

170
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,260
We're still in class, you know!

171
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:52,510
Sit down now!

172
00:08:52,510 --> 00:08:54,550
Aw, you're always so bossy!

173
00:08:54,550 --> 00:08:55,380
It's okay, it's okay!

174
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:55,840
It's not okay!
It's okay, it's okay!

175
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:56,720
It's not okay!

176
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,720
Well...

177
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,850
Hey, how were you chosen?

178
00:09:01,850 --> 00:09:03,430
Were there any tests?

179
00:09:03,430 --> 00:09:04,480
Weren't you scared?

180
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,350
What's the cockpit look like?

181
00:09:06,350 --> 00:09:09,110
Well, that's all secret.

182
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:13,440
Hey, what's the name of the robot?

183
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:16,860
I don't know much, but everyone
calls it Eva or Unit 01.

184
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:17,780
Eva?

185
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:18,950
And what's its ultimate attack?

186
00:09:18,950 --> 00:09:21,790
Some kind of knife.

187
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:25,040
It vibrates... An ultra-sonic wave...

188
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:27,790
That's amazing! You're the pride
of the school!

189
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:30,130
Yeah, right! Cool!

190
00:09:30,130 --> 00:09:32,800
And thus...

191
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,340
Oh...

192
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:36,260
That's all for today.

193
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,430
Ikari, where do you live?
All rise! Bow!

194
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:43,390
Hey, you guys, why don't you at least
show some manners at the end?

195
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:55,530
Sorry, transfer student,
but I've gotta beat you up!

196
00:09:55,530 --> 00:09:57,200
I won't feel right until I've smacked you.

197
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:04,950
Sorry, his little sister was injured
in the incident the other day.

198
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:07,290
Well, there you have it.

199
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:11,960
I'm not piloting it by choice either.

200
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:44,200
An emergency call.

201
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,910
I'll go on ahead.

202
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:56,840
A special state of emergency
has been declared

203
00:10:56,840 --> 00:11:00,880
for the Kanto and Chubu regions
surrounding the Tokai district.

204
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:03,970
All residents must evacuate to their
designated shelters immediately.

205
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:06,390
Repeating...

206
00:11:21,070 --> 00:11:22,610
The target has been sighted by our cameras.

207
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:24,280
It's already penetrated into
our territorial waters.

208
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:26,700
All personnel, assume
battle stations, Level One.

209
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:29,500
Roger, prepare for anti-aircraft interception.

210
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:32,620
New Tokyo-3 transforming
to battle formation.

211
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:34,790
Initiate accommodation of the central block.

212
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,240
Accommodation of central block

213
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:11,200
and the first through seventh districts
has been completed.

214
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,670
Notification of the government and other
related ministries, completed.

215
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:15,290
Target is still advancing.

216
00:12:15,290 --> 00:12:18,880
Present operational rate of anti-aircraft
interception: 48%.

217
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:21,380
What's the status of noncombatants
and civilians?

218
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:24,300
We've already received reports that
the evacuation has been completed.

219
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:26,340
Underground Shelter 334
Disaster Prevention Department, Tokyo-3

220
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:26,340
Total Floor Space

221
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:26,340
Maximum Capacity

222
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:28,180
Attention, elementary school and
junior high school students.

223
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:33,890
Please form groups with
your individual classes.

224
00:12:29,010 --> 00:12:33,730
<i>At noon today, a special emergency declaration was issued for the Kanto and Central regions centering on the Tokai area.
Details will be reported as they come in.</i>

225
00:12:32,390 --> 00:12:33,890
Not again!

226
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:36,350
Just text messages again?

227
00:12:36,350 --> 00:12:40,860
It's news censorship. They won't
show any of it to us civilians.

228
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:43,280
Even though it's an incredible event.

229
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:50,450
The fourth Angel would show up
while Commander lkari is away.

230
00:12:50,450 --> 00:12:52,080
It's a lot sooner than we expected.

231
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:54,330
The last time they gave us
a fifteen year break.

232
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:56,790
This time it's been only three weeks.

233
00:12:56,790 --> 00:12:59,170
They never care about
our convenience, do they?

234
00:12:59,170 --> 00:13:01,210
They're the type we women hate the most.

235
00:13:08,390 --> 00:13:10,890
It's a waste of the taxpayers' money.

236
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:14,310
The committee is demanding that
we dispatch an Evangelion again.

237
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,440
Those pesky bastards.

238
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,480
Even if they hadn't asked for it,
I'd have dispatched it anyway.

239
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:24,820
Entry procedure initiated.

240
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:26,780
LCL oxygenated.

241
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:28,410
Releasing airlock.

242
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:33,160
Why am I piloting this thing again,
even though my father's not here?

243
00:13:35,410 --> 00:13:37,370
Even though I got beat up?

244
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:44,630
Hey, I need to talk to you,
privately, you know?

245
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:45,510
What for?

246
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:47,470
Just give me a second, okay?

247
00:13:47,470 --> 00:13:48,720
Well, okay.

248
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:51,390
Class rep!

249
00:13:51,390 --> 00:13:52,140
What?

250
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:54,430
We both hafta go to the john!

251
00:13:54,430 --> 00:13:57,310
You were supposed to use the bathroom
before you came here.

252
00:13:57,810 --> 00:13:59,560
So, what's this about?

253
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:02,360
I've got to see it, at least once in my life.

254
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,730
You mean the battle up there?

255
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:07,240
Nobody knows when the enemy
will come the next time.

256
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,570
Kensuke, are you serious?

257
00:14:09,570 --> 00:14:12,240
If we let this opportunity escape us,
we may lose it forever!

258
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:15,200
Please, help me unlock the gate.

259
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,870
But you'll get killed if you go out there.

260
00:14:16,870 --> 00:14:18,790
You don't know if that'll happen,
even if we stay here.

261
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:21,000
If I could be killed anyway,
I'd rather see it first.

262
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,300
Idiot. What do you think Nerv's for?

263
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:27,130
And what is Nerv's most important weapon?

264
00:14:27,130 --> 00:14:29,510
It's the robot the new kid pilots.

265
00:14:29,510 --> 00:14:31,850
He protected us the other day,

266
00:14:31,850 --> 00:14:35,180
but you hit him pretty hard. Twice!

267
00:14:35,850 --> 00:14:40,150
If he refuses to pilot the robot,
we're all going to die.

268
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:44,690
Don't you have a duty to watch him fight?

269
00:14:44,690 --> 00:14:46,650
Ah, whatever.

270
00:14:47,650 --> 00:14:51,030
You sure are upfront about what you want,
ain't you?

271
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,120
Shinji, are you ready to head out?

272
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:56,870
Yes.

273
00:14:56,870 --> 00:15:01,830
Listen to me. Neutralize the enemy's AT field,
then fire a volley from the pallet gun.

274
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:03,840
Do it just like we practiced.
Can you handle that?

275
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,960
Yes.

276
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,130
Launch!

277
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:29,360
Cool! All my efforts really paid off!

278
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,820
Oh! This is what I've been waiting for!

279
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,210
There it is!

280
00:15:43,330 --> 00:15:45,420
The AT field has been deployed.
Target in the center, pull the switch.

281
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:47,960
Do it just as planned, okay, Shinji?
Target in the center, pull the switch.

282
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,050
Right.

283
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:58,100
You idiot! You hid the enemy
with your own smoke!

284
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:10,940
What the hell?! He's already losing!

285
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:11,950
It's all right.

286
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,610
I'm sending you a spare rifle.

287
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,240
Take it!

288
00:16:16,490 --> 00:16:18,870
Shinji? Shinji?

289
00:16:19,410 --> 00:16:21,250
Oh, man!

290
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:23,790
Being beaten up must have
really messed him up.

291
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:25,000
Shut up!

292
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:48,150
The umbilical cable's been severed!

293
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,530
Eva has switched to its internal
battery power source.

294
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:54,490
4 minutes, 53 seconds
of activation remaining.

295
00:17:02,870 --> 00:17:04,120
It's comin' this way!

296
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:11,760
Shinji, are you all right? Shinji!

297
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:12,590
Damage report?

298
00:17:12,590 --> 00:17:14,170
No problems detected. He can make it.

299
00:17:24,770 --> 00:17:26,770
Shinji's classmates?

300
00:17:26,770 --> 00:17:27,980
What are they doing there?

301
00:17:40,530 --> 00:17:42,410
Why won't he fight?

302
00:17:42,410 --> 00:17:44,620
Because we're here?

303
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:46,580
He can't move because of us!

304
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:50,290
Unit 01 activation time remaining,
3 minutes 28 seconds.

305
00:17:52,550 --> 00:17:55,380
Shinji, let them into the cockpit!

306
00:17:56,930 --> 00:17:59,470
Once you've got them,
make a temporary retreat.

307
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:00,510
We'll regroup!

308
00:18:00,510 --> 00:18:04,310
You think you can allow unauthorized
civilians into the entry plug?!

309
00:18:04,890 --> 00:18:06,350
I'm authorizing it.

310
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:08,270
You're exceeding your authority,
Captain Katsuragi!

311
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:13,360
Unit 01's remaining activation time,
3 minutes.

312
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:17,950
Hold Eva on your current commands
and eject the entry plug. Hurry up!

313
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:23,330
You two! Get in! Hurry!

314
00:18:24,450 --> 00:18:26,040
What the... It's water?

315
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:28,500
My camera! My camera!

316
00:18:32,130 --> 00:18:34,300
Abnormal conditions occurring
in the nervous system!

317
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,760
Of course. It's because you've allowed
two foreign bodies into the plug.

318
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,180
They're introducing noise
in the nerve impulse systems!

319
00:18:45,850 --> 00:18:47,640
Now! Retreat!

320
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:55,440
<i><i>Recovery route 34, retreat to
the east side of the mountain.</i></i>

321
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:56,480
Hey, new kid, she said, "Retreat!"

322
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:59,070
I mustn't run away. I mustn't run away.
New kid!

323
00:18:59,070 --> 00:19:00,240
I mustn't run away!

324
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:02,660
Progressive Knife engaged!

325
00:19:06,410 --> 00:19:09,210
Obey my orders, Shinji! You've got to retreat!

326
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:10,710
Shinji!

327
00:19:15,710 --> 00:19:16,840
That idiot...

328
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:38,480
Unit 01, activation time
remaining, 30 seconds!

329
00:19:39,030 --> 00:19:41,280
28... 27...

330
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,740
26... 25...

331
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:50,040
14... 13...

332
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:51,830
12... 11...

333
00:19:51,830 --> 00:19:53,920
10... 9...

334
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,670
8... 7...

335
00:19:55,710 --> 00:19:57,420
6... 5...

336
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:58,340
4...

337
00:19:58,380 --> 00:19:59,260
3...

338
00:19:59,260 --> 00:19:59,960
2...

339
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,090
1...

340
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:10,600
Eva Unit 01, activation ceased.

341
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,810
The target is completely silent.

342
00:20:55,140 --> 00:20:58,360
It's been three days.

343
00:20:59,020 --> 00:21:02,240
You mean, since we were chewed out?

344
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,570
No, since he stopped comin' to school.

345
00:21:05,570 --> 00:21:06,860
Who's "he"?

346
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:09,280
The new kid, the new kid.

347
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:11,740
I wonder what he's been doin' since then?

348
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:13,200
Are you worried about him?

349
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:16,170
No, not exactly worried.

350
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:18,840
Toji, for someone who's so tactless,
you're pretty stubborn.

351
00:21:19,590 --> 00:21:22,760
If you had apologized to him back then,

352
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,630
you wouldn't have had to agonize
over it for three days.

353
00:21:25,630 --> 00:21:28,260
Here, this is the new kid's phone number.

354
00:21:29,050 --> 00:21:31,180
If you're so worried, why don't you call him?

355
00:21:57,830 --> 00:22:00,880
To Be Continued

356
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,240
PREVIEW

357
00:23:06,730 --> 00:23:10,490
Unable to overcome his feelings,
Shinji even runs away from Misato.

358
00:23:10,490 --> 00:23:13,370
But the organization brings him
back without hesitation.

359
00:23:13,370 --> 00:23:15,620
There were no kind words waiting for him.

360
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:18,370
Next Evangelion:
"Rain, After Running Away"

361
00:23:18,370 --> 00:23:20,420
And of course, I'll give you lots
of fan service next time too!

362
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:21,370
RAIN, AFTER RUNNING AWAY
